// Spell's own app as a site:  a page per screen, each with a thumbnail of how it looks today.
// What opens over a page is a dialog or a sidebar, opened from the buttons above its thumbnail.
// Most addresses name a project, so they aren't in the navigation:  Home links to one of each.

home page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>open an example, a guide, a notebook or one of my projects from its card</story>
		<story "S2" done>start from a blank app, a small starter or Solitaire</story>
		<story "S3" done>make a project, an example or a guide from its group's header</story>
		<story "S4" done>bring back a project I exported</story>
	</stories>
	- to draw it:
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap spacing="s">
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the new project dialog}>New Project</button>
			<link link={"/edit/@spell/examples/Solitaire"}>The code editor</link>
			<link link={"/run/@spell/examples/Solitaire"}>A running app</link>
			<link link={"/edit/@spell/guides/SpellUI/Accordion/Usage.spell"}>A notebook</link>
			<link link={"/edit/@spell/guides/a-first-spell"}>A guide</link>
			<link link={"/site/@spell/examples/StarWarsSite"}>The site editor</link>
			<link link={"/apps/@spell/examples/TaskList"}>A hosted app</link>
		</stack>
		draw its thumbnail
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/home.jpg"

notebook page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>read a notebook, its words and its code in cells</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "notebook" is text
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/notebook.jpg"

guide page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>read a guide in the editor, its words as the comments of its spell file</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "guide" is text
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/guide.jpg"

code editor page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>change the code in its file tabs, with the running app beside it</story>
		<story "S2" done>see the program's output, its compiled code and what I can use, in the Program panel under the code</story>
		<story "S3" done>pick a part of the running app and change it in the Inspector</story>
		<story "S4" done>add a part from the palette</story>
		<story "S5" done>undo, save, discard my changes and publish a draft</story>
		<story "S6" done>move between Run, Edit and, for a site, Site</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "project" is text
	- to draw it:
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap spacing="s">
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the inspector sidebar}>Inspector</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the palette sidebar}>Palette</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the project settings dialog}>Project Settings</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the code settings dialog}>Code Editor Settings</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the project versions dialog}>Versions</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the new file dialog}>New File</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the duplicate project dialog}>Duplicate Project</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the change this dialog}>Change This</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the publish clash dialog}>Publish Clash</button>
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the person dialog}>You</button>
		</stack>
		draw its thumbnail
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/edit.jpg"

running app page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>use the program by itself, with no code showing</story>
		<story "S2" done>restart it</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "project" is text
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/run.jpg"

site editor page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>see a site's pages as a tree and a board of cards</story>
		<story "S2" done>drag a row to move a page, with its pages</story>
		<story "S3" done>change a page's name, title, address and state</story>
		<story "S4" done>write what a page must let people do, as stories</story>
		<story "S5" done>open a page's code from its card</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "project" is text
	- to draw it:
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap spacing="s">
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the site data sidebar}>Data</button>
		</stack>
		draw its thumbnail
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/site-pages.jpg"

theme editor page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>change a theme and see it on real pages</story>
		<story "S2" done>save it by name, to pick from every theme menu</story>
	</stories>
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/theme.jpg"

hosted app page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>use a program at its own address on Spell's cloud</story>
	</stories>
	// What the address names
	- its "project" is text
	- to draw it:
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap spacing="s">
			<button appearance="basic" onClick={show the sign-in dialog}>Sign In</button>
		</stack>
		draw its thumbnail
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/hosted-program.jpg"

terms page is a page:
	<stories>
		<story "S1" done>read Spell's terms</story>
	</stories>
	- its thumbnail is "snapshots/terms.jpg"

